# GoClaw — MVP tool contract

## Required interface

```go
type Tool interface {
    Name() string        // snake_case; name exposed to the model
    Description() string // shown to the model
    InputSchema() any    // JSON Schema for arguments
    Execute(ctx context.Context, input string) (Result, error)
}

type Result struct {
    Content string
    IsError bool  // true = user-visible failure (not a Go error)
}
```

**User-facing failures** → `Result{IsError: true, Content: msg}`, return `nil` error  
**System failures** → return non-nil `error` (bugs, unexpected I/O)

## Nine built-in tools (registered in `internal/app/run.go`)

### read_file
```
Name:   "read_file"
Input:  { "path": string, "offset_lines"?: int, "limit_lines"?: int }
Output: file contents
Cap:    512 KiB or 200 lines (whichever is smaller)
Risk:   read-only; workspace boundary + symlink resolution
```

### glob
```
Name:   "glob"
Input:  { "pattern": string }
Output: relative paths (slash-separated), max 500 matches
Risk:   read-only walk under workspace; basename-only patterns match any depth; path patterns use / for Match
```

### grep
```
Name:   "grep"
Input:  { "pattern": string (regexp), "path"?: string (file or dir under workspace) }
Output: path:line:content, max 200 matches; skips binary (NUL in prefix); 512 KiB read cap per file
Risk:   read-only under workspace
```

### bash
```
Name:   "bash"
Input:  { "command": string, "cwd"?: string }
Output: combined stdout + stderr
Cap:    256 KiB truncated; timeout default 30s (settings: bash_timeout_sec, max 3600)
Risk:   shell — expanded binary allowlist; single simple command (no pipes, ;, &&, redirects, $(...));
        quote-aware scan; quote URLs with &; Ask mode prompts before run
```

### web_fetch
```
Name:   "web_fetch"
Input:  { "url": string, "max_bytes"?: int }
Output: text / HTML body
Cap:    1 MiB default
Risk:   network — SSRF checks required, 30s timeout, max 5 redirects
```

### web_search
```
Name:   "web_search"
Input:  { "query": string }
Output: DuckDuckGo JSON — Answer, Definition, Abstract, Results (HTML stripped), RelatedTopics; empty → message with duckduckgo.com search URL
Cap:    up to 8 topical lines, 2 KiB per snippet (see limits.go)
Risk:   network
```

## LLM HTTP clients (`internal/llm`)

- Anthropic and Ollama streaming POSTs use **`doHTTPWithRetry`**: retry 429 / 503 / 504 (and transient network errors) with backoff; respect `Retry-After` when present.
- Do not add ad-hoc `http.Client.Do` loops in clients; extend `retry.go` if policy changes.

## Orchestrator loop budgets (do not change without consensus)
- Max LLM iterations per user message: **32**
- Max tool calls per user message: **64**

### write_file
```
Name:   "write_file"
Input:  { "path": string, "content": string }
Output: "wrote N bytes to path"
Cap:    1 MiB content (MaxWriteFileBytes)
Risk:   write — workspace boundary on parent dir (EvalSymlinks on parent, not file);
        atomic temp+rename; preserves existing file mode; stripped from ReadOnly profiles
```

### edit_file
```
Name:   "edit_file"
Input:  { "path": string, "old_string": string, "new_string": string, "replace_all"?: bool }
Output: "replaced N occurrence(s) in path"
Cap:    1 MiB result (MaxWriteFileBytes)
Risk:   write — exact str_replace; errors if old_string matches 0 or >1 times (unless replace_all:true);
        preserves file mode; atomic write; stripped from ReadOnly profiles
```

### todo_write
```
Name:   "todo_write"
Input:  { "merge": bool, "todos": [ { "content": string, "status": "pending|in_progress|completed", "activeForm": string } ] }
Output: snapshot of the current task list
Cap:    50 items max; 500 runes per content field
Risk:   session_meta — in-memory only; cleared on /new; snapshot injected into system prompt via WithTodoStore
```

## LLM HTTP clients (`internal/llm`)

- Anthropic and Ollama streaming POSTs use **`doHTTPWithRetry`**: retry 429 / 503 / 504 (and transient network errors) with exponential backoff (base 500ms, ceiling 5min, max 10 attempts); respect `Retry-After` when present.
- Do not add ad-hoc `http.Client.Do` loops in clients; extend `retry.go` if policy changes.

## Orchestrator loop budgets (do not change without consensus)
- Max LLM iterations per user message: **32**
- Max tool calls per user message: **64**

## Registration in `internal/app/run.go` (actual current location)

```go
reg := tools.New()
reg.Register(tools.NewReadFile(workdir))
reg.Register(tools.NewGlob(workdir))
reg.Register(tools.NewGrep(workdir))
reg.Register(tools.NewBashWithTimeout(cfg.BashTimeoutSeconds()))
reg.Register(tools.NewWriteFile(workdir))
reg.Register(tools.NewEditFile(workdir))
reg.Register(tools.NewWebFetch())
reg.Register(tools.NewWebSearch(tools.WebSearchOptions{}))
reg.Register(tools.NewTodoWrite(todoStore))
// MCP tools registered after: mcp.RegisterSessionTools(ctx, reg, mcpSess, srv.ID)
```

> Note: registration is in `internal/app/chat_wiring.go` (`PrepareChatRuntime`), not `main.go`.

## MCP tools (`mcp__<server_id>__<tool_name>`)
- Registered at startup for each server in `cfg.MCPServers` (stdio JSON-RPC subprocess).
- Stripped from `ReadOnly` profiles by `stripMCPNames` in the orchestrator.
- Each tool call routed through `mcp.ToolAdapter.Execute` → JSON-RPC `tools/call`.

